WEBVTT

00:00:14.600 --> 00:00:17.100
If this path is obstructed...

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:20.480
...we wouldn't be able to reach the heart,

00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:23.440
and we wouldn't be able to deliver
any oxygen or nutrients, either.

00:00:26.810 --> 00:00:29.980
N-No...

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:34.310
To think that the coronary arteries
could get completely clogged like this...

00:00:34.310 --> 00:00:36.190
These symptoms...

00:00:36.190 --> 00:00:39.270
This is a heart attack!

00:00:39.270 --> 00:00:44.560
At this rate, no oxygen will reach the heart,
and it will become necrotic!

00:00:44.560 --> 00:00:50.730
Just now, a serious incident occurred
within the coronary arteries.

00:00:50.730 --> 00:00:56.400
As of today, this body will meet its demise!

00:00:57.850 --> 00:01:00.770
Th-The body's functions...

00:01:00.770 --> 00:01:02.560
...are coming to a halt!

00:01:03.520 --> 00:01:06.350
It's the end of the world!

00:01:09.060 --> 00:01:10.350
Work...

00:01:10.350 --> 00:01:14.230
Please work, heart!

00:01:14.230 --> 00:01:16.230
I...

00:01:16.230 --> 00:01:18.730
I still...

00:01:18.730 --> 00:01:21.400
...s-still...

00:02:59.070 --> 00:03:05.030
EPISODE 13

00:02:59.070 --> 00:03:05.030
CARDIAC ARREST, REVIVAL, AND A CHANGE

00:03:00.440 --> 00:03:03.350
Let's all work together!
We're going to clear a path here!

00:03:03.350 --> 00:03:05.060
Three, two...

00:03:11.480 --> 00:03:14.310
No good! It's not budging an inch!

00:03:14.310 --> 00:03:15.600
Dammit!

00:03:15.600 --> 00:03:19.270
We've got oxygen, but we can't deliver it
to the heart? Who knew...

00:03:21.690 --> 00:03:24.100
It's over.

00:03:24.100 --> 00:03:26.900
The heart's stopped.

00:03:26.900 --> 00:03:28.190
Give it up.

00:03:28.190 --> 00:03:31.690
Waiting to die is all that's left
for this body to do.

00:03:35.020 --> 00:03:37.810
Wh-What are these jolts?

00:03:40.740 --> 00:03:41.780
"WELCOME TO THE LUNGS"

00:03:44.900 --> 00:03:46.650
What the cell is going on?

00:03:46.650 --> 00:03:48.060
Hey!

00:03:48.060 --> 00:03:49.650
Come and take a look at this!

00:03:51.270 --> 00:03:55.400
There's a crack in the rib
protecting the internal organs?

00:03:55.400 --> 00:03:59.230
Oh man, it's all over now for this body.

00:04:03.190 --> 00:04:06.060
Wh-What in the world...

00:04:11.560 --> 00:04:13.810
What's going on?

00:04:13.810 --> 00:04:15.850
S-Senpai!

00:04:15.850 --> 00:04:17.560
Look at that!

00:04:18.650 --> 00:04:23.400
It's blinking in time with each jolt?

00:04:23.400 --> 00:04:25.520
Chest compressions.

00:04:25.520 --> 00:04:28.100
Also known as "cardiac massages."

00:04:28.100 --> 00:04:30.560
A cardiopulmonary resuscitation procedure.

00:04:30.560 --> 00:04:36.650
It is performed in order to keep oxygen
flowing to the heart when it stops beating.

00:04:36.650 --> 00:04:44.060
Because great force is being applied to
the chest, the ribs can sometimes break.

00:04:44.060 --> 00:04:45.850
This body...

00:04:45.850 --> 00:04:47.650
...is trying to live.

00:04:47.650 --> 00:04:48.440
Huh?

00:04:48.440 --> 00:04:50.060
I have to go.

00:04:51.020 --> 00:04:52.520
Senpai?

00:04:52.520 --> 00:04:54.730
Now where are you going?

00:04:54.730 --> 00:04:56.730
Once the blood flow is restored...

00:04:56.730 --> 00:04:59.020
...we're going to deliver oxygen right away.

00:04:59.020 --> 00:05:00.440
That's...

00:05:00.440 --> 00:05:01.850
...our job!

00:05:01.850 --> 00:05:04.520
Wh-What are you talking about?

00:05:04.520 --> 00:05:07.400
This body is about to die!

00:05:07.400 --> 00:05:10.190
Work isn't exactly...

00:05:10.190 --> 00:05:12.600
That's right.

00:05:12.600 --> 00:05:16.600
This body can just die for all I care.

00:05:16.600 --> 00:05:19.560
Finally, we won't have to work anymore.

00:05:19.560 --> 00:05:22.730
Isn't that what you're all thinking, too?

00:05:22.730 --> 00:05:27.060
Or wait, do you actually want to go on
working in such an environment?

00:05:28.560 --> 00:05:32.230
I'm serious! I'm sick and tired of it all!

00:05:32.230 --> 00:05:34.270
Look at you.

00:05:34.270 --> 00:05:38.600
Still trying to work at a time like this.

00:05:38.600 --> 00:05:42.600
That's how deep this body's got
its hooks in you? Huh?

00:05:44.520 --> 00:05:47.350
We couldn't work if we wanted to
because it's going to die!

00:05:47.350 --> 00:05:50.020
So just sit back and shut up!

00:05:50.020 --> 00:05:51.940
That's irrelevant.

00:05:51.940 --> 00:05:53.850
What?

00:05:53.850 --> 00:05:57.350
We're being forced to work under a Code Black?

00:05:57.350 --> 00:06:01.730
We don't have to work anymore
because it's about to die?

00:06:01.730 --> 00:06:03.810
All that's irrelevant!

00:06:05.350 --> 00:06:06.730
I...

00:06:06.730 --> 00:06:09.150
I work because I want to!

00:06:10.560 --> 00:06:11.850
With these hands...

00:06:11.850 --> 00:06:13.230
With these feet...

00:06:13.230 --> 00:06:15.850
I want to deliver oxygen!

00:06:15.850 --> 00:06:19.190
So, please... One more time...

00:06:19.190 --> 00:06:22.690
...start moving, heart!

00:06:22.690 --> 00:06:25.230
Move!

00:06:31.270 --> 00:06:33.150
Wh-What's going on?

00:06:33.150 --> 00:06:35.520
Did the heart just start moving?

00:06:37.980 --> 00:06:41.400
Does this mean
the pulse has been restored?

00:06:44.020 --> 00:06:46.900
No, it's just in a convulsive state!

00:06:46.900 --> 00:06:49.810
There's still no normal pulse!

00:06:49.810 --> 00:06:51.850
"Convulsive state"?

00:06:51.850 --> 00:06:53.900
Ventricular fibrillation.

00:06:53.900 --> 00:06:56.940
A condition in which the heart begins
to palpitate rapidly, or quiver,

00:06:56.940 --> 00:07:02.400
cutting off blood supply
to the entire body.

00:07:02.400 --> 00:07:05.480
A type of life-threatening arrhythmia.

00:07:06.810 --> 00:07:07.770
Fight.

00:07:07.770 --> 00:07:09.310
Huh?

00:07:09.310 --> 00:07:12.810
Fight... Fight... Fight!

00:07:12.810 --> 00:07:14.190
Fight?

00:07:14.190 --> 00:07:19.020
Fight! Fight! Fight!

00:07:15.940 --> 00:07:19.020
Fight! You can do it, heart!

00:07:19.020 --> 00:07:25.270
Fight! Fight! Fight!

00:07:26.730 --> 00:07:28.650
It's useless.

00:07:28.650 --> 00:07:37.770
Fight! Fight!

00:07:33.050 --> 00:07:35.260
"WHITE
BLOOD CELL"

00:07:37.770 --> 00:07:41.190
Fight.

00:07:41.190 --> 00:07:43.060
You can do it!

00:07:41.310 --> 00:07:44.440
"PLATELETS"

00:07:43.060 --> 00:07:44.310
Fight.

00:07:44.310 --> 00:07:46.940
Fight! Fight! Fight!

00:07:46.940 --> 00:07:49.060
Please give it your best shot.

00:07:49.060 --> 00:07:50.650
Fight!

00:07:50.650 --> 00:07:52.980
Fight, dammit!

00:07:52.980 --> 00:07:54.940
Please fight.

00:07:59.400 --> 00:08:02.230
Come back to life!

00:08:14.150 --> 00:08:17.230
Wh-What's going on?

00:08:17.230 --> 00:08:18.900
Now what's happening?

00:08:18.900 --> 00:08:22.980
Continuous stimulation is being applied
to the heart from outside!

00:08:29.270 --> 00:08:31.650
The heartbeat...

00:08:33.060 --> 00:08:34.690
Error, cleared!

00:08:34.690 --> 00:08:36.400
The ventricle has stopped fibrillating!

00:08:36.400 --> 00:08:39.150
The cardiorespiratory functions
have returned to normal!

00:08:43.290 --> 00:08:51.260
"PLEASE USE
IN CASE OF EMERGENCY"
"THE ALARM WILL GO OFF WHEN OPENED"

00:08:44.190 --> 00:08:45.940
AED.

00:08:45.940 --> 00:08:49.020
Automated External Defibrillator.

00:08:49.020 --> 00:08:52.850
A device that helps
restore the heart rhythm to normal

00:08:52.850 --> 00:08:55.980
by delivering electric shocks
to a heart that's fibrillating

00:08:55.980 --> 00:08:57.900
due to myocardial infarctions, etc.,

00:08:57.900 --> 00:09:02.480
and is no longer able to pump.

00:09:02.480 --> 00:09:04.770
What about the coronary artery blood clot?

00:09:04.770 --> 00:09:06.270
I-It's no good!

00:09:06.270 --> 00:09:09.310
The blood cells' route is still blocked!

00:09:12.100 --> 00:09:16.690
Either way, we won't be able
to ward off cardionecrosis!

00:09:16.690 --> 00:09:18.520
Dammit! Dammit!

00:09:18.520 --> 00:09:20.350
You think we're going to give up?

00:09:20.350 --> 00:09:25.310
It's our job to deliver oxygen
to the heart up ahead!

00:09:28.150 --> 00:09:29.940
What's that sound?

00:09:32.440 --> 00:09:33.810
Whoa!

00:09:35.350 --> 00:09:38.230
Wh-What the cell's that?

00:09:39.980 --> 00:09:41.020
Huh?

00:09:41.020 --> 00:09:42.940
It's starting to inflate!

00:09:42.940 --> 00:09:46.560
G-Get back! Everyone, evacuate!

00:10:05.350 --> 00:10:07.310
What the cell was that?

00:10:07.310 --> 00:10:09.440
A new type of germ?

00:10:09.440 --> 00:10:10.940
Hey, look!

00:10:11.940 --> 00:10:13.190
This is...

00:10:13.190 --> 00:10:17.190
The plaque's been pushed aside,
clearing the way?

00:10:17.190 --> 00:10:19.900
All right! Now we can get through!

00:10:19.900 --> 00:10:22.020
Oxygen! Deliver the oxygen!

00:10:22.020 --> 00:10:23.650
Right!

00:10:23.650 --> 00:10:26.150
To the heart! On the double!

00:10:26.150 --> 00:10:28.690
Th-The coronary artery's unblocked!

00:10:28.690 --> 00:10:30.270
Blood flow has been restored!

00:10:30.270 --> 00:10:33.150
Yeah!

00:10:33.150 --> 00:10:35.310
Stent treatment.

00:10:35.310 --> 00:10:39.560
A procedure in which a catheter is inserted
into the coronary artery,

00:10:39.560 --> 00:10:42.810
where a balloon is inflated to expand
a wire mesh tube called a "stent,"

00:10:42.810 --> 00:10:47.060
to open up clogged arteries.

00:10:47.060 --> 00:10:50.230
I-Idiots! It's too early to celebrate!

00:10:50.230 --> 00:10:51.480
Huh?

00:10:51.480 --> 00:10:54.850
If we don't get oxygen delivered across
the whole body as soon as possible,

00:10:54.850 --> 00:10:57.560
the cells will start
undergoing necrosis!

00:11:00.100 --> 00:11:04.440
Above all, if this brain is left
with any severe damage,

00:11:04.440 --> 00:11:06.650
the consequences will be dire.

00:11:10.020 --> 00:11:11.150
Hey there!

00:11:11.150 --> 00:11:12.810
We brought you some oxygen!

00:11:12.810 --> 00:11:14.980
Y-You guys!

00:11:14.980 --> 00:11:17.190
You mean we can pass
through the coronary artery again?

00:11:17.190 --> 00:11:20.230
That's right! For now, let's just
get this oxygen to the heart!

00:11:20.230 --> 00:11:22.100
Right! Let's get going!

00:11:22.100 --> 00:11:23.270
Okay!

00:11:24.190 --> 00:11:25.650
Way to go!

00:11:25.650 --> 00:11:28.100
It's all up to those Red Blood Cells...

00:11:28.100 --> 00:11:31.650
...whether or not this body makes it!

00:11:35.440 --> 00:11:37.650
The lights are back on!

00:11:37.650 --> 00:11:39.310
Senpai...

00:11:40.650 --> 00:11:43.730
Come on! The cells inside this body...

00:11:43.730 --> 00:11:46.020
...are waiting for this oxygen!

00:11:46.020 --> 00:11:47.100
Right!

00:11:53.650 --> 00:11:57.520
Sorry we're late!
We've come to deliver your oxygen!

00:12:00.980 --> 00:12:04.100
Huh? Gastric Chief Cell?

00:12:08.690 --> 00:12:10.850
What took you so long?

00:12:12.480 --> 00:12:14.440
Come on, guys! The oxygen's here!

00:12:14.440 --> 00:12:16.100
Take your positions!

00:12:16.100 --> 00:12:19.940
We've got tons of work backed up!
Don't stop! Just keep going!

00:12:19.940 --> 00:12:21.480
Right!

00:12:22.900 --> 00:12:24.650
For heaven's sake...

00:12:25.650 --> 00:12:30.520
I knew you'd come, AA2153.

00:12:30.520 --> 00:12:34.850
Hey! You're keeping the other cells
waiting, right? Get going!

00:12:34.850 --> 00:12:36.310
Right!

00:12:36.310 --> 00:12:39.400
Go on, take it!

00:12:39.400 --> 00:12:40.770
Right!

00:12:47.650 --> 00:12:50.650
Sorry to keep you waiting
for your oxygen!

00:12:50.650 --> 00:12:52.190
There you are.

00:13:03.100 --> 00:13:04.650
You really saved the day.

00:13:04.650 --> 00:13:09.100
Thanks to you guys, it looks like
the brain will be left with almost no damage.

00:13:11.060 --> 00:13:12.600
Thank goodness.

00:13:12.600 --> 00:13:14.900
Please accept my gratitude
on behalf of everyone.

00:13:14.900 --> 00:13:16.480
Thank you for all your hard work.

00:13:16.480 --> 00:13:19.900
No, we should be thanking you
for all that you do.

00:13:25.400 --> 00:13:28.650
Is everyone all right?
We've brought you some oxygen!

00:13:30.730 --> 00:13:33.650
Everyone, there's no time
for all this weeping!

00:13:33.650 --> 00:13:35.310
We need to get ready to open!

00:13:35.310 --> 00:13:36.940
Right!

00:13:36.940 --> 00:13:39.150
Don't worry about us.

00:13:39.150 --> 00:13:42.980
Please deliver that oxygen
to the more crucial organs.

00:13:42.980 --> 00:13:47.850
He's right. Even if some hair falls out,
it wouldn't be life-threatening.

00:13:47.850 --> 00:13:49.730
What are you talking about?

00:13:49.730 --> 00:13:53.770
We're going to make sure
that every cell in this body gets oxygen!

00:13:53.770 --> 00:13:56.230
Because that's our job!

00:13:59.560 --> 00:14:02.100
Much obliged.

00:14:02.100 --> 00:14:04.310
We've come to deliver your oxygen!

00:14:07.190 --> 00:14:10.060
Yay! Thank goodness!

00:14:10.060 --> 00:14:14.810
Well, this is unusual. I thought
the liver was known as the "silent organ."

00:14:14.810 --> 00:14:16.850
It's all good.

00:14:14.950 --> 00:14:16.200
TALKING IS STRICTLY FORBIDDEN

00:14:16.850 --> 00:14:20.480
When are we ever going to be happy if not now?

00:14:24.060 --> 00:14:25.940
So sorry I kept you waiting!

00:14:25.940 --> 00:14:27.810
I've brought you your oxygen!

00:14:30.020 --> 00:14:31.900
Y-You...

00:14:31.900 --> 00:14:34.730
I'm so glad you're safe.

00:14:34.730 --> 00:14:36.650
If you could stamp here, please.

00:14:38.850 --> 00:14:43.020
Thanks! Thank you!

00:14:43.020 --> 00:14:48.650
After all the times
I lashed out at you until now...

00:14:49.810 --> 00:14:51.480
Even so...

00:14:51.480 --> 00:14:56.270
...instead of abandoning me,
you're still bringing me oxygen.

00:14:56.270 --> 00:14:58.150
Because that's...

00:14:58.150 --> 00:15:01.060
That's our job.

00:15:01.060 --> 00:15:03.310
Please use this oxygen...

00:15:03.310 --> 00:15:05.600
...to work hard again!

00:15:10.350 --> 00:15:12.400
The cells...

00:15:12.400 --> 00:15:15.100
...are regaining their vigor!

00:15:15.100 --> 00:15:17.810
Okay, we're going to carry out
our own tasks, too!

00:15:17.810 --> 00:15:20.690
We're going to head to the site of infraction
and help out with the aftermath!

00:15:20.690 --> 00:15:22.150
Roger that!

00:15:30.100 --> 00:15:32.150
The light...

00:15:32.150 --> 00:15:34.520
...is spreading...

00:15:36.480 --> 00:15:41.270
One simple job.
Delivering oxygen every day.

00:15:41.270 --> 00:15:45.770
All the while getting yelled at
by our senpais and other cells.

00:15:45.770 --> 00:15:48.020
If you're a Red Blood Cell,

00:15:48.020 --> 00:15:51.940
then deliver, deliver,
deliver oxygen until you drop!

00:15:53.690 --> 00:15:57.310
No matter how hard we work...

00:15:57.310 --> 00:16:00.690
...our work environment
just keeps getting worse.

00:16:00.690 --> 00:16:05.100
I can't even count how many times
my life was in danger.

00:16:11.310 --> 00:16:14.150
No way!

00:16:14.150 --> 00:16:16.850
Everybody, run! Please run!

00:16:20.650 --> 00:16:24.350
There were times
when I lost sight of who I was.

00:16:24.350 --> 00:16:26.150
I've got to work hard.

00:16:27.400 --> 00:16:32.020
And it was driven home to me over and over
just how powerless I was.

00:16:32.020 --> 00:16:34.100
The hair is falling out!

00:16:44.190 --> 00:16:49.980
"ENUCLEATION CEREMONY"

00:16:45.980 --> 00:16:49.850
There were times
when I even bailed on my own job.

00:16:51.480 --> 00:16:53.190
I...

00:16:53.190 --> 00:16:55.270
...don't want to work anymore.

00:16:57.310 --> 00:17:02.400
So many times...
Over and over again, I questioned this job.

00:17:02.400 --> 00:17:04.230
But...

00:17:04.230 --> 00:17:06.350
...this is our job.

00:17:06.350 --> 00:17:10.770
Hey, what do you think you're doing? Hurry up!

00:17:07.230 --> 00:17:10.770
It's something that this body
can't do without.

00:17:10.770 --> 00:17:13.560
I can raise my head high
and take pride in it now!

00:17:15.150 --> 00:17:16.730
In this job!

00:17:39.190 --> 00:17:40.980
Everybody, this way!

00:17:40.980 --> 00:17:42.810
Watch your step, okay?

00:17:42.810 --> 00:17:44.350
Okay!

00:17:45.900 --> 00:17:49.350
Hello!

00:17:49.350 --> 00:17:52.690
Everyone's getting a lot done, huh?

00:17:52.690 --> 00:17:56.350
There haven't been
any carbon monoxide leaks lately...

00:17:56.350 --> 00:17:59.020
...and there's a lot less plaque
in the blood vessels...

00:17:59.020 --> 00:18:01.350
...so it's easier to transport oxygen now.

00:18:01.350 --> 00:18:03.020
True.

00:18:03.020 --> 00:18:06.270
The only unfortunate thing is that
since there's no more alcohol raining down,

00:18:06.270 --> 00:18:09.770
we don't have as many chances
to head to the liver to get detoxed, huh?

00:18:12.690 --> 00:18:15.900
It would be great if this could last.

00:18:19.520 --> 00:18:21.060
Yes.

00:18:23.600 --> 00:18:25.900
All right, I'm leaving that work to you, then!

00:18:25.900 --> 00:18:27.100
Okay!

00:18:30.730 --> 00:18:33.440
Whoa!

00:18:33.440 --> 00:18:35.900
Wh-White Blood Cell!

00:18:38.150 --> 00:18:41.560
It looks like you were battling
a pretty huge germ there.

00:18:41.560 --> 00:18:45.940
No worries. That was just
a generic resident flora.

00:18:47.730 --> 00:18:49.190
It's changed.

00:18:49.190 --> 00:18:53.980
Yes. Since that day, both blood flow
and nutritional status have improved,

00:18:53.980 --> 00:19:00.730
stress has been reduced, and it's a much
better environment for everyone to work in now.

00:19:00.730 --> 00:19:04.850
Deliver oxygen
and retrieve carbon dioxide.

00:19:04.850 --> 00:19:07.650
Nothing's changed about the tasks
that I have to carry out.

00:19:07.650 --> 00:19:09.060
But...

00:19:09.060 --> 00:19:13.020
In an environment like this,
I can work even harder than before!

00:19:16.400 --> 00:19:20.060
You might be the one
who's changed most of all, huh?

00:19:20.060 --> 00:19:20.980
Wha...

00:19:20.980 --> 00:19:22.940
You've sure grown up a lot.

00:19:22.940 --> 00:19:26.310
N-No way. I still have
a long way to go.

00:19:26.310 --> 00:19:28.600
The way I see it,
you're a full-fledged cell now.

00:19:28.600 --> 00:19:31.230
H-Hey, you're embarrassing me.

00:19:31.230 --> 00:19:32.560
But...

00:19:33.850 --> 00:19:38.310
I'm so thrilled to be acknowledged by you,
the one I've always looked up to!

00:19:43.980 --> 00:19:47.980
"Looked up to"? That's just...

00:19:47.980 --> 00:19:53.020
I mean, you're a Red Blood Cell
and I'm a White Blood Cell, so...

00:19:53.020 --> 00:19:56.690
I-I'm so sorry! Maybe "looked up to"
isn't the right phrase--

00:19:56.690 --> 00:19:59.230
Hey, Senpai!

00:19:59.230 --> 00:20:02.440
Where should I transport this package?

00:20:02.440 --> 00:20:05.600
Didn't I tell you earlier?

00:20:05.600 --> 00:20:06.850
Go with him.

00:20:06.850 --> 00:20:09.270
Oh, right.

00:20:10.600 --> 00:20:14.060
Hey, Senpai, what were you doing
to make you blush like that?

00:20:14.060 --> 00:20:17.270
Oh, uh, hey, this is just...

00:20:18.650 --> 00:20:22.400
This is the inside of a human body.

00:20:22.400 --> 00:20:24.650
Every day, we receive oxygen in the lungs...

00:20:24.650 --> 00:20:26.730
...and deliver it to the entire body.

00:20:26.730 --> 00:20:30.560
That's all there is to it. But...

00:20:30.560 --> 00:20:34.440
That's our job as Red Blood Cells.

00:20:31.450 --> 00:20:32.960
RECEIVED

00:20:34.440 --> 00:20:40.480
One by one, the jobs we cells do
may be insignificant, but...

00:20:40.480 --> 00:20:44.150
...with all the efforts of us cells at work,

00:20:44.150 --> 00:20:47.730
this body is able to live on!

00:22:23.350 --> 00:22:24.600
The vascular wall?

00:22:24.600 --> 00:22:26.560
You Red Blood Cells, stay back!

00:22:26.560 --> 00:22:28.060
Okay!

00:22:28.060 --> 00:22:30.020
Something's coming?

00:22:34.190 --> 00:22:37.100
It's sucking us in?

00:22:37.100 --> 00:22:38.810
White Blood Cell!

00:22:38.810 --> 00:22:41.310
Let me go or you'll get dragged into this, too!

00:22:41.310 --> 00:22:43.270
I'm not letting go!

00:22:44.770 --> 00:22:46.980
Red Blood Cell!

00:22:52.480 --> 00:22:56.020
Senpai! Senpai!

00:22:57.940 --> 00:23:04.400
Senpai! Thank goodness!
I was afraid you were never going to wake up!

00:23:04.400 --> 00:23:06.020
Where the cell are we?

00:23:06.020 --> 00:23:09.440
The subclavian vein, it says.

